{
 "id": "2024-kassab-levent",
 "name": "Levent and Ortabayır, Istanbul: Beauty and Safety (7-point)",
 "description": "Method replication: participants rate 24 street views from two neighbouring Istanbul districts, the business and villa district Levent and the dense residential Ortabayır, on beauty and safety from 1 (poor) to 7 (high). The images are not the paper's stimuli (52 Google Street View views fetched for this template inside each district, 26 per district, 2025 captures).\n\nOriginal study: Kassab & Uzun (2024), \"Quantifying the Visuo-Perceptual Segregation Between Ortabayır and Levent District in Istanbul through Semantic Segmentation\", Sakarya University Journal of Science 28(6), 1165–1177. Fifty raters scored 300 Yandex panorama images (150 per district, on Talatpaşa, Dutluk and cross streets in Ortabayır and Levent Street and its side streets in Levent) for beauty and safety on a 7-point scale in Google Forms; the scores were compared with semantic segmentation shares of buildings, pavement, vehicles, sky, nature, people and road.\n\nDifferences from the original study: (1) Google Street View instead of Yandex panoramas, sampled on a grid inside each district rather than on the named streets; (2) 24 randomly drawn images per participant instead of all 300; (3) the segmentation step is not part of the template.",
